From 77be12132b9cf3794f19de047f1197190fa1c099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Kumar Singh <ashishkmr472@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:49:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA:GPU] A compile can stop after buffer assignment and
 state its memory

EARLY_EXIT_POINT_AFTER_BUFFER_ASSIGNMENT (xla_gpu_experimental_early_exit) maps to the AOT
kAfterBufferAssignment, which no compiler implemented: the GPU compiler runs the HLO passes, cuDNN's compiler
passes (their workspaces are buffers), scheduling and the post-scheduling pipelines (ScheduleForBackend, shared
with CompileToBackendResult), then buffer assignment, and returns an EarlyExitCompilationResult holding the
assignment, whose GetCompiledMemoryStats states the compile's memory (CompiledMemoryStats::FromBufferAssignment,
the one owner GpuAotCompilationResult reads too), no code emitted. A planner reads an executable's memory at the
cost of its HLO passes alone.
